{
  "schema": "orca.head_envelope.v1",
  "id": "elegoo-neptune4",
  "name": "Elegoo Neptune 4 / 4 Pro / 4 Plus / 4 Max stock toolhead (dual-gear direct drive, front cover with two side 4015 part-cooling blowers, inductive probe rear-left, V-wheel carriage on X beam)",
  "provenance": "Elegoo Neptune 4 / 4 Pro / 4 Plus / 4 Max stock toolhead (dual-gear direct drive, front cover with two side 4015 part-cooling blowers, inductive probe rear-left, V-wheel carriage on X beam) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/758185-bambu-lab-hotend-kit-for-elegoo-neptune-4 (STEP with the stock 'ZSB N4P Hotend' sub-assembly: extruder housing, Elegoo PCB, LED, Level Sensor; plus a remix of the OrzOrzOrz shroud); https://www.printables.com/model/711424-elegoo-neptune-4promaxplus-fan-shroud-v5 (OrzOrzOrz V5 replacement shroud STEP, mounts on the stock housing; Plus/Max version 1.5 mm longer); https://www.printables.com/model/813810-elegoo-neptune-4promaxplus-fan-shroud-v5-with-beac (V5 + Beacon mount, used as a cross-check of nozzle height); https://www.printables.com/model/1104307 (N4/N4 Pro blank carriage plate, 84 mm wide) and https://www.printables.com/model/1446980 (Plus/Max carriage reference); https://github.com/OpenNeptune3D/OpenNept4une/blob/main/printer-confs/base.cfg ([probe] x_offset -24.25, y_offset 20.45); https://www.elegoo.com/products/hotend-kit-for-neptune-4-4-pro (hotend photos: heatsink/sock/nozzle proportions); https://www.elegoo.com/products/elegoo-neptune-4-pro-fdm-3d-printer (front render of head + 4x4020 aux fan bar; transparent-cover renders). Frame: nozzle tip at origin, +X right, +Y back, mm. No stock Elegoo CAD exists publicly; geometry is built from (a) the stock 'ZSB N4P Hotend' sub-assembly inside Printables 758185 (extruder housing, PCB, LED, Level Sensor) - its probe lands at x -24.5 / y +20.2 relative to the nozzle axis, matching Klipper [probe] x_offset -24.25 / y_offset 20.45, which validates the XY registration; (b) the OrzOrzOrz V5 shroud (711424), which registers onto the 758185 shroud's mounting section to 0.02 mm median, giving its placement on the stock housing; (c) Elegoo photos. Vertical datum: stock tip placed 3.6 mm above the Bambu-hotend tip of 758185 (photo of stock hotend scaled by the 35 mm heatsink top plate gives 51.4 mm heatsink-top-to-tip -> 2.9; Beacon-mount shroud 813810 implies ~4.4; chose 3.6). With that, stock probe bottom = 1.8 mm and the Orz duct bottom = 1.85 mm above tip; the stock cover bottom in Elegoo's front render sits at about tip level to ~2 mm above, so the lowest non-nozzle level is set to 1.5 mm (conservative). Stock cover is narrower than the Orz 5015 shroud: ~73 mm wide (front render, scale 0.171 mm/px from the 84 mm carriage plate and 60 mm wheel spacing), flat bottom ~57 mm wide; Y extents of the cover use the Orz CAD (same mounting) with margin. Heater sock bottom ~5.0 mm above tip (exposed nozzle measured 5.2 mm from Elegoo photo). Gantry: the N4/N4 Pro aux fan bar (4x4020) under the X beam is the binding gantry obstacle at ~7.5 mm; the Plus/Max use a different aux fan (6025) and their beam alone is ~52 mm, but one conservative profile is shipped for all four. Plus/Max hotend (ceramic heater, brass block) is ~1.5 mm longer with a matching longer cover, so clearances relative to the tip are taken as equal. Footnote: vertical numbers carry ~+/-1 mm photo uncertainty; margins of 0.3-0.5 mm were applied toward the tip. parts: per-component boxes without the 0.3 mm engine margin; 'derived' parts come from the community CAD of the stock sub-assembly (Printables 758185) placed with the tip datum above; estimated parts are extended by their photo uncertainty. The stock cover bottom has a ~24 mm wide, ~3 mm tall notch around the nozzle at the front, so the centre bridge starts ~4.3 mm while the duct lips either side reach ~1.2-1.5 mm. Nozzle: land radius 0.50 mm, 40.0-degree cone to Z=2.00, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 7.50 mm above the tip, Y 26.0..70.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/elegoo-neptune4.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
